<title>FRANCE: PARIS BOURSE.</title>
<headline>PARIS BOURSE.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>French shares were volatile in early business, following Wednesday's roller-coaster session, and was going in and out of the red after a slightly higher opening. Dealers said there remained uncertainty over the government's economic and budget policies. &quot;We are near the all-time high and the prospect of higher taxes for companies is clearly negative -- the market is fragile,&quot; a broker said.</p>
<p>* CAC-40 index up 16.4, or 0.56 percent, at 2,925.85 at 0831 GMT</p>
<p>* CAC-40 July futures 2,928 vs 2,917 at Wednesdays close.</p>
<p>* Broader SBF120 index up 9.44 at 1,992.27</p>
<p>* Volume was 1.2 billion francs</p>
